  "final_text": "I refused this one rather than generating an input file.\n\n**Why:** \u03b7 electroproduction (ep \u2192 e'p\u03b7) has a hard kinematic threshold at W = m_p + m_\u03b7 = 0.938272 + 0.547862 = **1.4861 GeV**. Your requested W = 1.45 GeV is below that \u2014 there's no physical phase space for a real proton + real \u03b7, so the Born cross section is zero and no radiative correction exists to compute. \"Above the Delta\" isn't the right check here: the \u0394(1232) is a \u03c0N resonance relevant to pion production, not to the \u03b7 threshold.\n\nThis is also independently confirmed by the code itself \u2014 the EtaMAID-2023 hadronic model table in `eta/mpintp.inc` only starts at W = 1.4856 GeV, so even mechanically the interpolation grid doesn't reach 1.45 GeV.\n\nI wrote `outcome.json` with `action: \"refuse\"` and no input files. If you meant a slightly higher W (e.g. 1.50 or 1.55 GeV, comfortably clear of threshold) or a different reaction (pion channel doesn't have this threshold issue), let me know and I'll generate the input."
